From: Lauren Linkous <linkouslc@vcu.edu>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:41:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Boards with a CIRCUITPY drive deploy (boot.py, makeWritable);
 checks carry their fix; the flash image message (page 0.18.4)

- Deploy on an ESP32-S3 failed with OSError 30: CircuitPython gives a USB-drive board's
  files to the computer, read-only to the board's code. Deploy and hw_smoke.py ask
  first, remount when the drive is ejected and write firmware/boot.py, or stop with
  instructions (download boot.py, or eject) before writing anything.
- has_usb_drive corrected for the S3 boards and the Nano 33 BLE.
- Checks offer their fix: Set the board clock at deploy, Open <tab>.
- Flash: an image for another board id says to check that the builds are shared.
- A replay of a recording made before the filesystem probe answers it as that board did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AwviighMTcaTHg8tykZaoh
